{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794363290904,"sessionID":"ses_e37ac4e01ffeXNi8x5cqzCz6dT","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_eb39f04454c44aa68996bfed","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"echo \"HOME=$HOME\"; mkdir -p \"$HOME/tmpwork\" && python3 -m venv \"$HOME/tmpwork/venv\" && \"$HOME/tmpwork/venv/bin/pip\" install -q -r /workspace/backend/requirements.txt -c /workspace/backend/requirements.lock 2>&1 | tail -3; \"$HOME/tmpwork/venv/bin/python\" -c \"import flask, gunicorn; print('flask', flask.__version__)\"","timeout":240000},"output":"HOME=/run/home\nERROR: Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some requirements. Here is a list of those requirements along with the hashes their downloaded archives actually had. Add lines like these to your requirements files to prevent tampering. (If you did not enable --require-hashes manually, note that it turns on automatically when any package has a hash.)\n    flask==3.1.3 --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, gunicorn; print('flask', flask.__version__)\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'\n","metadata":{"output":"HOME=/run/home\nERROR: Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some requirements. Here is a list of those requirements along with the hashes their downloaded archives actually had. Add lines like these to your requirements files to prevent tampering. (If you did not enable --require-hashes manually, note that it turns on automatically when any package has a hash.)\n    flask==3.1.3 --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"<string>\", line 1, in <module>\n    import flask, gunicorn; print('flask', flask.__version__)\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nModuleNotFoundError: No